From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:08:18 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: clpc: account for GPU demand on T6040

Apply DjDeveloperr's GPU-demand mechanism from d69f14f4e4fb to T6040.
The CPU-only policy can leave the fabric low during GPU-only work. Enable
its graphics demand input and describe the existing graphics PMGR state
in DT, as T8140 and T8132 already do.

Use T6040's existing DCS 5 / fabric 2 table, not T8140's state numbers.
CPU demand keeps its three-sample sustain rule; graphics demand uses the
shared hold and idle release. No voltage, ceiling, parameter or new
platform option is introduced. Confirm powered-state tracking and idle
floor release on J616s before qualifying the performance result.

Link: https://github.com/aurora-silicon/linux/pull/440
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
[j604: dropped hunk for arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6040.dtsi, absent in 1.604]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c b/drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c
index 007b8a3301..50b4eed1bd 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c
@@ -630,6 +630,8 @@ static const struct apple_clpc_hw apple_clpc_hw_t8140 = {
  * A cluster requests only after three busy samples in a row (12 ms). At idle
  * a single busy sample raised the floor about 60 % of the time, from short
  * bursts of background work; three in a row bring that to about 11 %.
+ * GPU demand bypasses the CPU streak and uses the same qualified DCS 5 /
+ * fabric 2 states until the graphics state powers off and HOLD_MS expires.
  */
 static const struct apple_clpc_hw apple_clpc_hw_t6040 = {
 	.rail = { [APPLE_CLPC_DCS] = 0, [APPLE_CLPC_SOC] = 1 },
@@ -638,6 +640,7 @@ static const struct apple_clpc_hw apple_clpc_hw_t6040 = {
 		[APPLE_CLPC_SOC] = { 0, 1, 2, 2 },
 	},
 	.sustain = 3,
+	.gpu_demand = true,
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id apple_clpc_of_match[] = {
